{"persona": {"name": "Maya Chen", "role": "Senior Software Engineer", "company": "Lumenary Systems", "summary": "Backend-focused developer on the integrations team, currently migrating a legacy event pipeline to Kafka. She works from home in Austin, uses a MacBook Pro, and tends to start late after a slow morning.", "workday": {"start": "09:45", "end": "18:30", "lunch": "13:00"}}, "people": [{"key": "dana", "name": "Dana Whitfield", "role": "Engineering Manager", "channel": "slack"}, {"key": "priya", "name": "Priya Raghavan", "role": "Staff Engineer, Integrations", "channel": "slack"}, {"key": "marcus", "name": "Marcus Bell", "role": "Product Manager", "channel": "slack"}, {"key": "tom", "name": "Tom Okafor", "role": "DevOps Engineer", "channel": "slack"}, {"key": "jules", "name": "Jules Fontaine", "role": "Data Analyst (client side)", "channel": "email"}, {"key": "lena", "name": "Lena Park", "role": "Friend from college", "channel": "messages"}, {"key": "grandma", "name": "Grandma Ruth", "role": "Family", "channel": "messages"}], "threads": [{"key": "kafka_migration", "title": "Kafka migration for event pipeline", "kind": "main", "arc": "Monday: Maya picks up ticket EV-482 to move the order-events topic from the old RabbitMQ bridge. Tuesday: she hits a serialization issue with the Avro schema and posts in #integrations; Priya suggests reusing the existing schema registry subject. Wednesday: she writes a migration script and runs it against staging, but the consumer lag spikes. Thursday: she fixes the consumer group offset reset and coordinates with Tom to deploy the new bridge. Friday: PR #1187 is approved and merged; she updates the runbook and closes EV-482."}, {"key": "consumer_group", "title": "Consumer group naming decision", "kind": "decision", "arc": "Monday: Maya proposes naming consumer groups by service and environment (e.g. `order-sync-prod`). Tuesday: Marcus pushes back, wanting a version suffix. Wednesday: she creates a short comparison doc and polls the team in Slack. Thursday: the team votes 4-2 for `order-sync-prod-v2` style. Friday: she updates the migration script and the runbook to use the new convention."}, {"key": "invoice_question", "title": "Invoice question from Jules at Northwind Analytics", "kind": "correspondence", "arc": "Tuesday: Jules emails Maya asking why invoice #INV-22904 is missing from the exported dataset. Wednesday: Maya checks the pipeline logs and finds the event was dropped due to a malformed timestamp. Thursday: she sends Jules a corrected CSV and explains the fix. Friday: Jules confirms the invoice now appears and asks for a small schema change; Maya adds it to the backlog."}, {"key": "weekend_plans", "title": "Weekend trip to Fredericksburg", "kind": "personal", "arc": "Monday: Lena texts Maya about booking a cabin for the weekend. Tuesday: Maya checks Airbnb and sends Lena two options. Wednesday: they book the cabin (reservation #HB-88231) and split the cost. Thursday: Maya texts Grandma Ruth to ask if she wants to join for Saturday wine tasting. Friday: Grandma says yes, and Maya adds a stop at the wildflower farm to the itinerary."}, {"key": "side_project", "title": "Side project: recipe scraper", "kind": "side_project", "arc": "Maya tinkers with a small Python script to scrape recipes from a cooking site. Monday: she refactors the parser to use BeautifulSoup. Wednesday: she gets blocked by a Cloudflare challenge and tries using Playwright. Friday: she gets it working for a few test URLs and commits it to a private GitHub repo."}], "apps": ["slack", "vscode", "terminal", "zoom", "messages", "mail", "notes", "chatgpt", "spotify", "finder", "calendar", "preview", "notion"], "sites": ["github.com", "docs.google.com", "mail.google.com", "grafana.example.com", "confluence.lumenary.dev", "airbnb.com", "openai.com"], "noise": {"slack_titles": ["#integrations", "#incidents", "#random", "Dana Whitfield (direct message)", "Priya Raghavan (direct message)"], "pages": [{"host": "github.com", "title": "lumenary/event-bridge · Pull Request #1187", "path": "/lumenary/event-bridge/pull/1187"}, {"host": "docs.google.com", "title": "Consumer Group Naming - Lumenary", "path": "/document/d/1abc123/edit"}, {"host": "mail.google.com", "title": "Invoice #INV-22904 missing from export - Jules Fontaine", "path": "/mail/u/0/#inbox"}, {"host": "airbnb.com", "title": "Cabin in Fredericksburg, TX - reservation #HB-88231", "path": "/rooms/99887766"}, {"host": "confluence.lumenary.dev", "title": "Runbook: Kafka Event Bridge", "path": "/display/ENG/Runbook+Kafka+Event+Bridge"}]}}

Plan workday 4 (Friday) as JSON {"blocks": [...], "summary": "2-3 sentences of what happened"}.
What happened on earlier days: ["Day 1: Tuesday was a mixed day: Maya dug into the Kafka migration and hit a consumer lag spike after running the staging script, which she worked through with Tom. She also handled Jules's invoice question by finding the malformed timestamp and sending a corrected CSV, while the consumer group naming debate moved toward a team vote. In between, she booked the Fredericksburg cabin with Lena, got Grandma Ruth on board for wine tasting, and made progress on the recipe scraper with a Playwright workaround.", "Day 2: Wednesday was the day the Kafka migration finally went live: Maya coordinated with Tom on the staging lag, deployed the new bridge to prod after a quick Zoom call, and merged PR #1187. She also locked in the consumer group naming convention in the runbook, replied to Jules about the schema change, and made a small breakthrough on the recipe scraper with a cookie fix. The Fredericksburg trip got more concrete with Grandma's pickup time and a dinner plan, though the scraper's image download is still a loose end.", "Day 3: Thursday was a steady day: Maya verified the Kafka bridge was stable in prod, updated the runbook with the consumer group naming convention, and replied to Jules about the schema change. She also made a real breakthrough on the recipe scraper by getting image downloads working with Playwright, and finalized the Fredericksburg itinerary with Lena and Grandma Ruth."]

Each block: {"start": "HH:MM", "thread": one of ['consumer_group', 'invoice_question', 'kafka_migration', 'side_project', 'weekend_plans'], "noise": true|false, "steps": [...]}.
Steps (in order):
- {"do": "app", "app": <key from slack, vscode, terminal, xcode, zoom, messages, mail, notes, chatgpt, claude, spotify, finder, figma, calendar, preview, excel, keynote, notion>, "about": "what window/document", "min": minutes}
- {"do": "page", "host": "<site>", "about": "what page", "min": minutes, "new_tab": optional bool}
- {"do": "search", "about": "what they googled"}
- {"do": "type", "where": <app key or "web:<host>">, "intent": "what they write, to whom, and whether they send it",
   "sent": true|false, "to": "<person name if a message/email>"}
- {"do": "idle", "min": minutes, "about": "lunch / walk / away"}
Make it a real day: 9-16 blocks, threads interleaved, meetings (zoom/calendar), messages that interrupt, distraction
browsing, something left unfinished, something read but not answered, an abandoned tab. Keep each thread's arc moving.
Typing happens wherever it really would: Slack, email in the browser, Google Docs, notes, terminals, AI chat apps.

